# Footnotes: a call [^id] in the text and its Footnote, placed at the bottom of the page under a rule.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Footnotes · A footnote
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 15mm
	Section:
		Text: Footnotes
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: A footnote
		Paragraph: The call `[^id]` goes in a text with `Markup: markdown`, attached to the word. The `Footnote` with that `Id` can be written anywhere in the section and takes no room there. The engine numbers it and places it at the bottom of the page, under a rule.
			Style: intro
		Paragraph: Sales grew by 12% in the quarter[^source], above the forecast, and the margin stayed at 31%.
		Footnote:
			Id: source
			Paragraph: Figures from the annual report, closed on December 31.
		Paragraph: The rest of the page stays as it is: the note takes room only at the bottom.
